[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946108794","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116673#issuecomment-3946108794","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116673","id":3946108794,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rNNd6","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T17:15:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T17:15:35Z","body":"High level note: the additional (and extremely lengthy) descriptions on these functions are IMO a good indication that these should be separate functions, even if they do a lot of similar things under the hood. Especially the state within a state with the download and load phases is particularly gross API design.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3946108794/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3952908001","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116673#issuecomment-3952908001","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116673","id":3952908001,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rnJbh","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T15:24:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T15:24:14Z","body":"I think there's a risk that the simplified API becomes more cumbersome to use and has more pitfalls that might be hard to notice, the necessity to use `load_threaded` and being unable to use `@GDScript.load` feels like a big constraint just to avoid new API\r\n\r\nBased on what I can tell is the workflow in the original PR the way to do general loading would be largely unchanged for your basic actions and usage, with some additional API calls to handle invoking loading of async resources\r\n\r\nWhile I haven't tested either implementation in practical use I feel that having just some dedicated fetch and install code running specifically on Web with minimally intrusive code and then just loading as usual for all practical load code with no additional adjustments feels less complex and intrusive than adding new API for this, especially if there's a requirement to adjust to use threaded loading operations universally for those cases. The threaded load operation would take a bit of overhead to use to replace any normal `load` calls etc. especially if one doesn't want to use that for other platforms\r\n\r\nAnd I agree with the above that the need to clarify this is a good argument for dedicated API\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3952908001/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3953190615","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116673#issuecomment-3953190615","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116673","id":3953190615,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7roObX","user":{"login":"dom-crazygames","id":263700249,"node_id":"U_kgDOD7e_GQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263700249?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames","html_url":"https://github.com/dom-crazygames","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dom-crazygames/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T16:10:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T16:10:25Z","body":"This is looking good - is it possible to add an API for getting the amount of downloaded bytes? The big issue that this initiative solves is players churning during load times - lower load times are obviously the best case (less time for the players to get bored and leave!) but a crucial addition is **visible progress**. If the player can see what's going on/how long is left,  particularly with a solid number that they can see ticking upwards, they are less likely to churn.  ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3953190615/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3966511258","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116673#issuecomment-3966511258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116673","id":3966511258,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sbCia","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T13:05:53Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T13:06:09Z","body":"> This is looking good - is it possible to add an API for getting the amount of downloaded bytes? The big issue that this initiative solves is players churning during load times - lower load times are obviously the best case (less time for the players to get bored and leave!) but a crucial addition is **visible progress**. If the player can see what's going on/how long is left, particularly with a solid number that they can see ticking upwards, they are less likely to churn.\r\n\r\nThe current PR do tell the download progress using `ResourceLoader.load_threaded_get_status()`. There's no way to get how it relates to bytes downloaded though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3966511258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967350680","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116673#issuecomment-3967350680","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116673","id":3967350680,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sePeY","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T15:27:55Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T15:27:55Z","body":"Added @mihe and @syntaxerror247 as reviewers as I am touching the way platform code is shared.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3967350680/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4513063893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116673#issuecomment-4513063893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116673","id":4513063893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDP_j1Q","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T21:50:44Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T21:50:44Z","body":"FYI, these changes get this PR building for me:\r\n\r\n```patch\r\ndiff --git a/editor/export/editor_export_platform_utils.cpp b/editor/export/editor_export_platform_utils.cpp\r\nindex 63f2d3dc967..2d9f262235c 100644\r\n--- a/editor/export/editor_export_platform_utils.cpp\r\n+++ b/editor/export/editor_export_platform_utils.cpp\r\n@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@\r\n #include \"core/extension/gdextension.h\"\r\n #include \"core/io/file_access_encrypted.h\"\r\n #include \"core/io/file_access_pack.h\"\r\n+#include \"core/io/resource_loader.h\"\r\n #include \"core/math/random_pcg.h\"\r\n #include \"core/version.h\"\r\n #include \"editor/export/editor_export_platform.h\"\r\ndiff --git a/platform/web/emscripten_helpers.py b/platform/web/emscripten_helpers.py\r\nindex ba8cd382c82..3d8f5388602 100644\r\n--- a/platform/web/emscripten_helpers.py\r\n+++ b/platform/web/emscripten_helpers.py\r\n@@ -43,8 +43,8 @@ def package_js_module_action_ensure_copyright_buffer(target, source, env, filena\r\n     target = target[0]\r\n     source = source[0]\r\n \r\n-    with open(source, mode=\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as source_file:\r\n-        with open(target, mode=\"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as target_file:\r\n+    with open(source.get_abspath(), mode=\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as source_file:\r\n+        with open(target.get_abspath(), mode=\"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as target_file:\r\n             new_contents = process_file_buffer_copyright_buffer(filename, source_file)\r\n             CHUNK_SIZE = 1024\r\n             while True:\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4513063893/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"r